um-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-08-02","finding":"Janitorial duties: This standard was evaluated as part of a DFPS investigation and found deficient.     During pick up times staff are observed cleaning in the classroom which leads to less attention to the children in care as they are being picked up.","topic":"sanitation","source_record_id":"1026664678","violation_type_title":"Janitorial duties (26 TAC §746.1203(3)(C))","topic_label":"Sanitation & hygiene"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94689-i20240613-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2202-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-94689-i20240613","date":"2024-06-13","original_code":"746.2202(4)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-08-02","finding":"Planned activities designed to meet special care needs-Integrated activities: This standard was evaluated as part of a DFPS investigation and found deficient.     Based on information provided a child with special care needs was said to be put to the side in the classroom or outside on the playground and not included as part of day to day activities.","topic":"facilities","source_record_id":"1026672588","violation_type_title":"Planned activities designed to meet special care needs-Integrated activities (26 TAC §746.2202(4))","topic_label":"Facilities & equipment"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94689-i20240613-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-94689-i20240613","date":"2024-06-13","original_code":"746.1201(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-08-02","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control: This standard was evaluated as part of a DFPS investigation and found deficient.     Based on information provided a caregiver did not conduct a face to name accounting of children or maintain the documentation of transitions as required by the operation. This caused the caregiver to be unaware of the number of children they were responsible for and a child to be left outside on the playground.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026671518","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control (26 TAC §746.1201(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94689-i20240613-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1205-a-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-94689-i20240613","date":"2024-06-13","original_code":"746.1205(a)(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-08-02","finding":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity: This standard was evaluated as part of a DFPS investigation and found deficient.     Based on information provided, a child with special care needs, that requires additional individual attention to maintain their safety, was left on the playground alone for 5-8 minutes","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026671517","violation_type_title":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity (26 TAC §746.1205(a)(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94689-i20240613-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1205-a-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-94689-i20240613","date":"2024-06-13","original_code":"746.1205(a)(2)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-08-02","finding":"Responsibilities of Caregivers - Know number of children responsible for: This standard was evaluated as part of a DFPS investigation and found deficient.     Based on information provided it was determined that the caregivers responsible for a group of children did not keep